<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
<Content>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. HOYT HOUSE - KENDRA&#x27;S ROOM - EVENING</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SUPER: EARLIER. HALE RIVER, ALABAMA. 2014.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A small room. The window unit labors. Tops on the bed, three deep. BRIANNA, 16, round-faced and sure of herself, her hair done and her shoes already on, sits cross-legged on the bed with Kendra&#x27;s phone, scrolling. KENDRA HOYT, 16, her father&#x27;s long frame already, headphones around her neck, is half inside the closet.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>This one?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She holds up a top. Brianna does not look up.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Yeah.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You didn&#x27;t look.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Brianna looks.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Yeah. That one.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Or this.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>That&#x27;s a church top.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>It is not a church top. I wore it to the thing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You wore it to church and then to the thing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kendra throws it on the bed with the others and goes back in. Brianna goes back to the phone.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Marcus is going.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>From inside the closet:</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Who said.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Tasha said Keisha said. Keisha&#x27;s in Darnell&#x27;s fourth period, and Darnell sits by Marcus, and Darnell told Keisha he was going because Marcus asked him was he going. So he&#x27;s going.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kendra comes out with a third top and holds it against herself in the mirror on the closet door. Brianna is behind her in the mirror, still on the phone.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Marcus asked Darnell.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>No. Marcus asked Jalen was Darnell going, and Jalen asked Darnell, and Darnell said he&#x27;d go if Marcus was going, and Jalen told Marcus that, and Marcus said then he&#x27;d go. So they&#x27;re both going. Because of each other.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kendra turns the top one way and the other in the mirror.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He sits in front of me third period and every time she passes papers back he turns all the way around. Every time. He&#x27;s got nothing to say, he just turns around.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Brianna puts the phone down.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He&#x27;s looking at you.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He&#x27;s looking at Tasha.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Tasha sits by the door.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kendra looks at herself with the top a while longer.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>This one.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>That one. Did your daddy say he&#x27;s driving?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kendra pulls the top she has on off over her head and the new one on. The next lines come through fabric.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He&#x27;s driving.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>My mama&#x27;s going to call him.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>She called Miss Ondine.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>She called Miss Ondine and Miss Ondine talked to her forty-five minutes about her hip.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kendra&#x27;s head comes out of the new top.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Which hip.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I don&#x27;t know which hip, Kendra.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The front door, off. Boots on the floor. Brianna is off the bed before Kendra is, and hands her the phone on the way past.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT (O.S.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Kendra.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>In here.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. HOYT HOUSE - KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>AMOS HOYT, 40s, Black, lean, in a work shirt with the sleeves rolled, sets a toolbox down inside the door and goes to the sink. He runs the water and starts on his hands with the bar soap. The girls come in behind him. Brianna sits at the table without being asked. Kendra stops in the doorway in the new top.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Hi, Mr. Hoyt.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Brianna. Your mama find Ondine?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Yes sir. They talked about her hip.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Which hip.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I don&#x27;t --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nobody knows which hip, Daddy.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He shuts the water off and turns with the towel, and sees the two of them. The top.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>What are y&#x27;all into.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nothing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>That&#x27;s a lot of nothing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>We&#x27;re going to the movies. You said.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I said I&#x27;d drive. What movie.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kendra comes the rest of the way in and leans on the counter beside him.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>The scary one. Everybody&#x27;s going.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Who&#x27;s everybody.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Everybody.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Tasha, and Darnell, and Marcus, and --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Everybody.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Marcus.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He opens the refrigerator and stands in it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>That&#x27;s the Shelby boy. I put a belt on his mama&#x27;s dryer. He stood in that laundry room the whole time I was down on the floor and never once handed me a thing. I&#x27;d say hand me that, and he&#x27;d look at it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He&#x27;s shy.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He&#x27;s something.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Daddy.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I&#x27;m saying what I saw.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He takes out the tea and pours a glass. Drinks half of it standing there.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>What time&#x27;s it start.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Seven-thirty.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He pulls out the chair across from Brianna and sits down with the glass, the first time he has sat since he came in.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I might go see that.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>No.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BRIANNA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He could sit in the back.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Brianna.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I&#x27;ll sit in the back. I&#x27;ll sit with Marcus. Hand him some popcorn, see does he take it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Brianna laughs. Kendra doesn&#x27;t, and then does. She is the only one standing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You&#x27;re driving. You&#x27;re not going in.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>We&#x27;ll see what I do.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He gets up with the tea and heads for the hall. In the doorway he turns back and looks at the top again.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You going in that?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>What&#x27;s wrong with it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nothing&#x27;s wrong with it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He looks at it a second longer than that.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Seven-thirty.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KENDRA</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Seven-thirty.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>HOYT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Then somebody better start supper. I ain&#x27;t driving nobody hungry.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Kendra is already at the refrigerator before he has finished saying it. He goes down the hall. Brianna stays where she is at the table, like she lives there.</Text></Paragraph>
</Content>
</FinalDraft>
